    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a high-upside slate today, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (78.74) and **Andy Pages** (70.49), both benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against Kochanowicz (5.12 xERA). **Kyle Tucker** is our premier play, as his combination of elite talent and a soft-tossing matchup creates the highest ceiling in the lineup. **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) also serves as a high-value piece; despite a baseline projection that suggests mediocrity, his batting order position (#1) and favorable wind conditions at the park vault him into a Strong category start. We are closely monitoring the status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez**, as their scores hover in the high-50s; while they remain in the lineup, they are essentially tethered to the assumption that they land in advantageous spots against Eduardo Rodriguez.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Curtis Mead** (52.75). He posted a solid score and was seriously considered for a utility spot, but he ultimately fell victim to the optimizer's preference for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.69) despite the latter's tougher matchup against Bradish. The primary concern across the board remains the high volume of \"Lineup Pending\" designations; specifically, **Josh Jung** (55.75) and **Jackson Merrill** (51.21) carry risk if they are dropped in the batting order, as their scores are heavily sensitive to those order-based multipliers. We are particularly cautious about **Dominic Smith** (41.36), whose efficiency sits dangerously close to our \"Below Floor\" threshold of 40; if his lineup spot drops or late-breaking weather reports emerge, we may look to move **Brayan Rocchio** or **Coby Mayo** into the mix, though **Coby Mayo** was specifically benched today for failing to clear the efficiency bar.",
